{"id": 1917201, "name": "VON LEHE v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.", "name_abbreviation": "Von Lehe v. Atlantic Coast Line R. R.", "decision_date": "1907-09-11", "docket_number": "6654", "first_page": "168", "last_page": "169", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "78 S.C. 168"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "34 Stat. 81", "category": "laws:leg_session", "reporter": "Stat.", "opinion_index": 0}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 96, "char_count": 1003, "ocr_confidence": 0.636, "sha256": "88ba086115352b11a56f5315ead81ac362c91b719037c8993b17a3ed6adb3801", "simhash": "1:5bc6dc65dc2d1cd2", "word_count": 174}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T22:14:03.106788+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["VON LEHE v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nMr. Justice Woods.\nThe plaintiff recovered judgment ini a magistrate\u2019s court for the value of two sacks of grist and two sacies of flour shipped from Nashville, Tenn., to plaintiff at Walterboro, S. C., and the statutory penalty of fifty dollars. The judgment was affirmed by the Circuit Court and the defendant appeals solely on the ground that the penalty statute of 1903 (34 Stat. 81) is unconstitutional. The question has been settled by the case of Charles v. R. R. Co., ante, 36.\nThe judgment of this Court, is that the judgment of the Circuit Court be affirmed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Woods."}], "attorneys": ["Mr. W. Huger Pitssimons for appellant, Mr. J. S. Griffin, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "6654\nVON LEHE v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.\nEuled by case of Charles v. JR. R. Co., ante, 36'.\nBefore Purdy, ]., Colleton,\nFebruary, 1907.\nAffirmed.\nAction by A. Von Relie against Atlantic Coast Ri\u00f1e R. R. Co. From order of Circuit Court affirming judgment of Magistrate J. E. Bryan, defendant appeals.\nMr. W. Huger Pitssimons for appellant, Mr. J. S. Griffin, contra.\nSeptember 11, 1907."}, "file_name": "0168-01", "first_page_order": 180, "last_page_order": 181}